<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0235">Example <span data-tag="0235">4.3.6.5</span>.</a> Let $f: A \hookrightarrow A'$ be a right anodyne morphism of simplicial sets. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="018J" href="/tag/018J">4.3.6.4</a> to the inclusion $\emptyset \hookrightarrow \Delta ^0$, we deduce that the natural map $A^{\triangleright } \coprod _{A} A' \hookrightarrow A'^{\triangleright }$ is inner anodyne. Similarly, if $g: B \hookrightarrow B'$ is left anodyne, the induced map $ B' \coprod _{B} B^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow B'^{\triangleleft }$ is inner anodyne. </p>
